---
import RosterEaseLayout from "../layouts/RosterEaseLayout.astro";
---

<RosterEaseLayout
  title="On your device"
  description="RosterEase processes imports on-device. Understand what stays local and what optional Calendar, Maps, backups and support features share."
>
  <div class="re-shell">
    <section class="re-page-intro">
      <p class="re-kicker">On your device</p><h1>
        Your imports stay<br />on your device.
      </h1><p>
        Your roster and client imports are read and organised on your iPhone or
        iPad. Their contents are not sent to a third-party AI service for
        processing.
      </p>
    </section><article class="re-prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Stored and processed locally</h2><p>
          Roster, workplace, client, visit and preference data is stored
          locally. Text recognition and import parsing run on-device. There is
          no RosterEase account to create, no advertising and no app analytics.
        </p><p>
          Your core plan and import processing do not need a RosterEase server.
          Optional online features, app distribution and purchases still use
          Apple services.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Optional sharing</h2><p>
          You can share information through these features. Each destination has
          its own privacy settings.
        </p><dl class="re-data-list">
          <div>
            <dt>Shift Worker Calendar sync</dt><dd>
              Writes schedule information to the calendar you select. Private
              shift notes are excluded unless you enable their inclusion. Your
              calendar provider and sharing settings determine who can see those
              events.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Maps and travel estimates</dt><dd>
              Use address or location text for directions or optional estimates.
              Client names and private notes are not included in those requests.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Backup files</dt><dd>
              You start an encrypted, passphrase-protected export and choose
              where it goes. RosterEase does not keep a backend copy. A file
              provider you choose has its own storage and retention rules.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Support and diagnostics</dt><dd>
              Diagnostics can be previewed locally and shared by you. Email
              support receives what you send. Redact examples before sharing
              them.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Apple and TestFlight</dt><dd>
              Apple handles distribution and purchases. TestFlight can provide
              the developer with crash reports, tester information and feedback
              under Apple's terms. Apple device backup is separate from a
              RosterEase export.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>For work where privacy matters.</h2><p>
          People working in health or community care can import a roster without
          uploading it to a cloud AI service.
        </p><p>
          Use only information your organisation permits on your device. Keep
          client details to what you need for planning, and check workplace
          rules before enabling Calendar sharing, using Maps or saving a backup
          with a provider.
        </p><p>
          RosterEase is a personal planner, not a clinical record system. We do
          not claim healthcare compliance or approval for a particular
          workplace. Suitability also depends on device security, permitted use
          and your organisation's requirements.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Data settings and support</h2><p>
          <a href="/help/calendar-and-privacy"
            >Calendar, Maps and privacy settings</a
          ><br /><a href="/help/backup-and-restore">Backup and restore guide</a
          ><br /><a href="/privacy">Full Privacy Policy</a>
        </p><p>
          Need a clearer explanation for your workplace? <a href="/contact"
            >Ask us about the app's data handling.</a
          >
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</RosterEaseLayout>
